  "review_notes": [
    "Reconciliation patch: *unto* moved from `ποιήσω` to `Ἰησοῦν`, matching the chapter's uniform treatment of supplied case prepositions.",
    "The distinction the chapter draws is recorded as a convention: a particle that is part of the English lexical gloss of the Greek verb stays with the verb (*ask for*, *rail on*, *witness against*, *took off*), while a preposition that only marks an expressed complement's case goes with that complement."
